title: "Protein Studio: A Blender-like molecular viewer with an embedded Python scripting console"
type: software
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-10-21"
authors:
  - family-names: Xie
    given-names: Zhengwei
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9572-878X"
    affiliation: "Peking University International Cancer Institute, Health Science Center, Peking University, Beijing, China"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kekegg/protein-studio"
url: "https://github.com/kekegg/protein-studio"
abstract: >-
  Protein Studio is a desktop molecular visualisation and editing application
  with an embedded Python scripting console, built on PySide6, PyVista and
  VTK. It loads PDB structures and renders seven representations (cartoon,
  ribbon, ball-and-stick, surface, points, electrostatic surface and hydrogen
  bonds) under seven colour schemes, including an AlphaFold pLDDT palette.
  Secondary structure is inferred from backbone hydrogen bonds, so
  structure-aware colouring works on PDB files that carry no HELIX or SHEET
  records. It reads MD trajectories, docking poses and AlphaFold predictions,
  runs OpenMM free-energy perturbation sweeps with checkpoint/resume, and
  exposes a Model Context Protocol server so that an AI agent can drive the
  viewer over stdio or HTTP.
keywords:
  - molecular visualization
  - protein structure
  - PDB
  - PySide6
  - PyVista
  - free energy perturbation
  - Model Context Protocol
  - AlphaFold pLDDT
